<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsoede</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Edegi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsoede, also called Edegi, is the legendary founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe Kingdom</a> in the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> valley of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. Nupe tradition makes him a son of an Attah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igala">Igala</a> by a Nupe mother, who travelled up the Niger, united the Nupe chiefdoms in the early 16th century and founded a capital at Gbara. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> figures and other regalia attributed to him were long kept as royal relics.</p></div>
